Powers of xvals can be calculated once in transformed data and referred to in the model block. Again, you would want to do orthogonal polynomials rather than raw polynomials.

The other thing you would want to do is use the loop from t = 2 to T to build up the three linear predictors and then after that loop call

target += normal_lpdf(a | a_hat, sigma_a);
target += normal_lpdf(b | b_hat, sigma_b);
target += normal_lpdf(x | x_hat, sigma);

which allocates less memory.

